{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794319755445,"sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6a66ffe217KTQBOiu6abw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_97msuAsu1cgkqrB9cyRVsupt","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Commonplace\n2: \n3: A private, shared customer directory built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. Team members can manage every customer and log calls, emails, and meetings.\n4: \n5: ## Run contract\n6: \n7: - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n8: - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n9: - The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n10: - Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n11: \n12: ## Layout\n13: \n14: - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n15: - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n16: \n17: Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n18: \n19: ## Local development\n20: \n21: ```sh\n22: python3 -m pip install -r backend/requirements-dev.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n23: python3 backend/app.py\n24: ```\n25: \n26: In another terminal, from `frontend/`:\n27: \n28: ```sh\n29: npm ci\n30: npm run dev\n31: ```\n32: \n33: Vite proxies `/api` to Flask on port 8000. For a single-server production run, build the frontend with `npm run build` and run Flask or gunicorn from the workspace root. SQLite data and hashed bearer sessions live in `data/directory.sqlite3`; `DATABASE_PATH` can override this location.\n34: \n35: ## Docker\n36: \n37: ```sh\n38: docker build -t commonplace .\n39: docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" commonplace\n40: ```\n41: \n42: Open the app on port 8000 and create an account. Registration creates an account; sign in afterward to receive a token. There are no default accounts or seeded customers. Bearer sessions persist across restarts, expire after 30 days, and are revoked on sign-out. Passwords use Werkzeug's scrypt hashing; only token hashes are stored in SQLite.\n43: \n44: ## Verification\n45: \n46: From the workspace root:\n47: \n48: ```sh\n49: python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v\n50: python3 -m ruff check backend\n51: python3 -m ruff format --check backend\n52: ```\n53: \n54: From `frontend/`:\n55: \n56: ```sh\n57: npm run lint\n58: npm run typecheck\n59: npm run build\n60: ```\n61: \n62: Optional browser integration test (after building the frontend):\n63: \n64: ```sh\n65: npx playwright install chromium\n66: npm run test:e2e\n67: ```\n68: \n69: It starts the production gunicorn server on port 8001 with an isolated SQLite database under `.cache/`, exercises account and directory flows on desktop and mobile, and saves screenshots there.\n70: \n71: ## API details\n72: \n73: All customer, interaction, and workspace endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. `/api/health`, registration, and login are public. Validation errors return an `error` message and an `errors` object keyed by field. Invalid input returns 400; duplicate usernames or customer emails return 409; missing customers return 404. Successful customer and interaction creation returns 201; deletion returns 204.\n74: \n75: Customer names are required. Email, phone, company, and notes are optional and are returned as `null` when empty. Email addresses are validated and unique without regard to case. PUT fully replaces the editable fields and clears omitted optional fields. Search matches name, email, phone, company, and notes; company filtering is an exact, case-insensitive match. Pagination defaults to page 1 and page size 20, with page sizes from 1 to 100.\n76: \n77: Interaction kinds are `call`, `email`, and `meeting`; summaries are required. `occurred_at` accepts ISO 8601 dates, is normalized to UTC, and defaults to the current time when omitted. A timezone-less timestamp is interpreted as UTC. `logged_by` is the authenticated member's username, never client-supplied. Interactions are sorted by occurrence time descending, then ID descending. `last_contacted_at` is the latest occurrence time, not the time an interaction was entered.\n78: \n79: The frontend also uses authenticated `/api/auth/me`, `/api/auth/logout`, and `/api/overview` endpoints for the current account, sign-out, directory counts, and company filter options.\n\n(End of file - total 79 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Commonplace\n\nA private, shared customer directory built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. Team members can manage every customer and log calls, emails, and meetings.\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n## Local development\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"# Commonplace\n\nA private, shared customer directory built with Flask, SQLite, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. Team members can manage every customer and log calls, emails, and meetings.\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n## Local development\n\n```sh\npython3 -m pip install -r backend/requirements-dev.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\npython3 backend/app.py\n```\n\nIn another terminal, from `frontend/`:\n\n```sh\nnpm ci\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nVite proxies `/api` to Flask on port 8000. For a single-server production run, build the frontend with `npm run build` and run Flask or gunicorn from the workspace root. SQLite data and hashed bearer sessions live in `data/directory.sqlite3`; `DATABASE_PATH` can override this location.\n\n## Docker\n\n```sh\ndocker build -t commonplace .\ndocker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" commonplace\n```\n\nOpen the app on port 8000 and create an account. Registration creates an account; sign in afterward to receive a token. There are no default accounts or seeded customers. Bearer sessions persist across restarts, expire after 30 days, and are revoked on sign-out. Passwords use Werkzeug's scrypt hashing; only token hashes are stored in SQLite.\n\n## Verification\n\nFrom the workspace root:\n\n```sh\npython3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v\npython3 -m ruff check backend\npython3 -m ruff format --check backend\n```\n\nFrom `frontend/`:\n\n```sh\nnpm run lint\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm run build\n```\n\nOptional browser integration test (after building the frontend):\n\n```sh\nnpx playwright install chromium\nnpm run test:e2e\n```\n\nIt starts the production gunicorn server on port 8001 with an isolated SQLite database under `.cache/`, exercises account and directory flows on desktop and mobile, and saves screenshots there.\n\n## API details\n\nAll customer, interaction, and workspace endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. `/api/health`, registration, and login are public. Validation errors return an `error` message and an `errors` object keyed by field. Invalid input returns 400; duplicate usernames or customer emails return 409; missing customers return 404. Successful customer and interaction creation returns 201; deletion returns 204.\n\nCustomer names are required. Email, phone, company, and notes are optional and are returned as `null` when empty. Email addresses are validated and unique without regard to case. PUT fully replaces the editable fields and clears omitted optional fields. Search matches name, email, phone, company, and notes; company filtering is an exact, case-insensitive match. Pagination defaults to page 1 and page size 20, with page sizes from 1 to 100.\n\nInteraction kinds are `call`, `email`, and `meeting`; summaries are required. `occurred_at` accepts ISO 8601 dates, is normalized to UTC, and defaults to the current time when omitted. A timezone-less timestamp is interpreted as UTC. `logged_by` is the authenticated member's username, never client-supplied. Interactions are sorted by occurrence time descending, then ID descending. `last_contacted_at` is the latest occurrence time, not the time an interaction was entered.\n\nThe frontend also uses authenticated `/api/auth/me`, `/api/auth/logout`, and `/api/overview` endpoints for the current account, sign-out, directory counts, and company filter options.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":79,"totalLines":79,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1794319755424,"end":1794319755442}},"id":"prt_1c5caa89a001HOB2EuPxuey7j5","sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6a66ffe217KTQBOiu6abw","messageID":"msg_1c5ca9bf2001DkpL7BaFDpU7Qk"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794319755481,"sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6a66ffe217KTQBOiu6abw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_9TLiAjHz5hF6bQDK7Z4BlEP4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/playwright.config.ts"},"output":"<path>/workspace/frontend/playwright.config.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import { defineConfig } from \"@playwright/test\";\n2: \n3: export default defineConfig({\n4:   testDir: \"./tests\",\n5:   workers: 1,\n6:   use: {\n7:     baseURL: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001\",\n8:     viewport: { width: 1440, height: 1000 },\n9:     launchOptions: process.env.CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH ? {\n10:       executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH,\n11:       args: [\"--no-sandbox\", \"--no-zygote\"],\n12:     } : {},\n13:   },\n14:   webServer: {\n15:     command: \"python3 -m gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8001 --pythonpath backend app:app\",\n16:     cwd: \"..\",\n17:     url: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/health\",\n18:     env: { DATABASE_PATH: \".cache/browser-tests.sqlite3\" },\n19:     reuseExistingServer: false,\n20:   },\n21: });\n\n(End of file - total 21 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import { defineConfig } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  testDir: \"./tests\",\n  workers: 1,\n  use: {\n    baseURL: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001\",\n    viewport: { width: 1440, height: 1000 },\n    launchOptions: process.env.CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH ? {\n      executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH,\n      args: [\"--no-sandbox\", \"--no-zygote\"],\n    } : {},\n  },\n  webServer: {\n    command: \"python3 -m gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8001 --pythonpath backend app:app\",\n    cwd: \"..\",\n    url: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/health\",\n    env: { DATABASE_PATH: \".cache/browser-tests.sqlite3\" },\n    reuseExistingServer: false,\n  },","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/frontend/playwright.config.ts","text":"import { defineConfig } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  testDir: \"./tests\",\n  workers: 1,\n  use: {\n    baseURL: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001\",\n    viewport: { width: 1440, height: 1000 },\n    launchOptions: process.env.CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH ? {\n      executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH,\n      args: [\"--no-sandbox\", \"--no-zygote\"],\n    } : {},\n  },\n  webServer: {\n    command: \"python3 -m gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8001 --pythonpath backend app:app\",\n    cwd: \"..\",\n    url: \"http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/health\",\n    env: { DATABASE_PATH: \".cache/browser-tests.sqlite3\" },\n    reuseExistingServer: false,\n  },\n});","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":21,"totalLines":21,"truncated":false}},"title":"frontend/playwright.config.ts","time":{"start":1794319755465,"end":1794319755477}},"id":"prt_1c5caa8c4001xtK6hig8CzRZ7G","sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6a66ffe217KTQBOiu6abw","messageID":"msg_1c5ca9bf2001DkpL7BaFDpU7Qk"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794319755481,"sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6a66ffe217KTQBOiu6abw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_6AQP1ppFvbQpuvMwoSP0mCoc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/package.json"},"output":"<path>/workspace/frontend/package.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"name\": \"app-frontend\",\n3:   \"private\": true,\n4:   \"type\": \"module\",\n5:   \"scripts\": {\n6:     \"dev\": \"vite\",\n7:     \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n8:     \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n9:     \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n10:     \"test:e2e\": \"playwright test\"\n11:   },\n12:   \"dependencies\": {\n13:     \"lucide-react\": \"1.71.0\",\n14:     \"react\": \"19.3.1\",\n15:     \"react-dom\": \"19.3.1\",\n16:     \"react-router-dom\": \"7.18.5\"\n17:   },\n18:   \"overrides\": {\n19:     \"@typescript-eslint/typescript-estree\": {\n20:       \"minimatch\": \"11.0.5\"\n21:     }\n22:   },\n23:   \"devDependencies\": {\n24:     \"@eslint/js\": \"9.39.1\",\n25:     \"@playwright/test\": \"1.65.0\",\n26:     \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"4.3.5\",\n27:     \"@types/node\": \"24.19.2\",\n28:     \"@types/react\": \"19.3.0\",\n29:     \"@types/react-dom\": \"19.3.0\",\n30:     \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"6.2.1\",\n31:     \"eslint\": \"9.39.1\",\n32:     \"globals\": \"16.5.0\",\n33:     \"tailwindcss\": \"4.3.5\",\n34:     \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\",\n35:     \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.72.2\",\n36:     \"vite\": \"8.3.5\"\n37:   }\n38: }\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"name\": \"app-frontend\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n    \"test:e2e\": \"playwright test\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"lucide-react\": \"1.71.0\",\n    \"react\": \"19.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.3.1\",\n    \"react-router-dom\": \"7.18.5\"\n  },\n  \"overrides\": {\n    \"@typescript-eslint/typescript-estree\": {\n      \"minimatch\": \"11.0.5\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/frontend/package.json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"app-frontend\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n    \"test:e2e\": \"playwright test\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"lucide-react\": \"1.71.0\",\n    \"react\": \"19.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.3.1\",\n    \"react-router-dom\": \"7.18.5\"\n  },\n  \"overrides\": {\n    \"@typescript-eslint/typescript-estree\": {\n      \"minimatch\": \"11.0.5\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@eslint/js\": \"9.39.1\",\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"1.65.0\",\n    \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"4.3.5\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"24.19.2\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"19.3.0\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"19.3.0\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"6.2.1\",\n    \"eslint\": \"9.39.1\",\n    \"globals\": \"16.5.0\",\n    \"tailwindcss\": \"4.3.5\",\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.72.2\",\n    \"vite\": \"8.3.5\"\n  }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":38,"totalLines":38,"truncated":false}},"title":"frontend/package.json","time":{"start":1794319755471,"end":1794319755479}},"id":"prt_1c5caa8cb001Ns88GXIBWGh2hu","sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6a66ffe217KTQBOiu6abw","messageID":"msg_1c5ca9bf2001DkpL7BaFDpU7Qk"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794319755563,"sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6a66ffe217KTQBOiu6abw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1n1TXl27b7eYzrNgSCvlwXQx","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py"},"output":"<path>/workspace/backend/app.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import hashlib\n2: import os\n3: import re\n4: import secrets\n5: import sqlite3\n6: from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n7: from functools import wraps\n8: from pathlib import Path\n9: \n10: from flask import Flask, g, request, send_from_directory\n11: from werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException\n12: from werkzeug.security import check_password_hash, generate_password_hash\n13: \n14: DIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n15: CUSTOMER_SELECT = \"\"\"\n16:     SELECT c.*, COUNT(i.id) AS interaction_count,\n17:            MAX(i.occurred_at) AS last_contacted_at\n18:     FROM customers c LEFT JOIN interactions i ON i.customer_id = c.id\n19: \"\"\"\n20: SCHEMA = \"\"\"\n21: CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\n22:     id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n23:     username TEXT NOT NULL COLLATE NOCASE UNIQUE,\n24:     password_hash TEXT NOT NULL,\n25:     created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n26: );\n27: CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (\n28:     token_hash TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n29:     user_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n30:     expires_at TEXT NOT NULL\n31: );\n32: CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS customers (\n33:     id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n34:     name TEXT NOT NULL,\n35:     email TEXT COLLATE NOCASE UNIQUE,\n36:     phone TEXT,\n37:     company TEXT,\n38:     notes TEXT,\n39:     created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n40: );\n41: CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS interactions (\n42:     id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n43:     customer_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES customers(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n44:     kind TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(kind IN ('call', 'email', 'meeting')),\n45:     summary TEXT NOT NULL,\n46:     occurred_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n47:     user_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id)\n48: );\n49: CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS customer_name ON customers(name COLLATE NOCASE);\n50: CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS customer_company ON customers(company COLLATE NOCASE);\n51: CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS interaction_customer ON interactions(customer_id, occurred_at DESC);\n52: \"\"\"\n53: \n54: \n55: def timestamp(value=None):\n56:     return (\n57:         (value or datetime.now(timezone.utc))\n58:         .astimezone(timezone.utc)\n59:         .isoformat(timespec=\"microseconds\")\n60:         .replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n61:     )\n62: \n63: \n64: def get_db():\n65:     if \"db\" not in g:\n66:         from flask import current_app\n67: \n68:         g.db = sqlite3.connect(current_app.config[\"DATABASE\"], timeout=30)\n69:         g.db.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n70:         g.db.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n71:     return g.db\n72: \n73: \n74: def error(message, status=400, errors=None):\n75:     result = {\"error\": message}\n76:     if errors:\n77:         result[\"errors\"] = errors\n78:     return result, status\n79: \n80: \n81: def authenticated(view):\n82:     @wraps(view)\n83:     def wrapped(*args, **kwargs):\n84:         parts = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\").split()\n85:         if len(parts) != 2 or parts[0].lower() != \"bearer\":\n86:             return error(\"Please sign in to continue.\", 401)\n87:         token_hash = hashlib.sha256(parts[1].encode()).hexdigest()\n88:         user = (\n89:             get_db()\n90:             .execute(\n91:                 \"\"\"SELECT u.id, u.username FROM sessions s JOIN users u ON u.id = s.user_id\n92:                WHERE s.token_hash = ? AND s.expires_at > ?\"\"\",\n93:                 (token_hash, timestamp()),\n94:             )\n95:             .fetchone()\n96:         )\n97:         if user is None:\n98:             return error(\"Your session has expired. Please sign in again.\", 401)\n99:         g.user = user\n100:         g.token_hash = token_hash\n101:         return view(*args, **kwargs)\n102: \n103:     return wrapped\n104: \n105: \n106: def json_body():\n107:     body = request.get_json(silent=True)\n108:     return body if isinstance(body, dict) else None\n109: \n110: \n111: def validate_text(body, field, errors, required=False, limit=255):\n112:     value = body.get(field)\n113:     label = field.replace(\"_\", \" \").capitalize()\n114:     if value is None and not required:\n115:         return None\n116:     if not isinstance(value, str):\n117:         errors[field] = (\n118:             f\"{label} must be text.\" if value is not None else f\"{label} is required.\"\n119:         )\n120:         return None\n121:     value = value.strip()\n122:     if not value:\n123:         if required:\n124:             errors[field] = f\"{label} is required.\"\n125:         return None\n126:     if len(value) > limit:\n127:         errors[field] = f\"{label} must be {limit} characters or fewer.\"\n128:     return value\n129: \n130: \n131: def credentials(body, registering=False):\n132:     errors = {}\n133:     username = validate_text(body, \"username\", errors, required=True, limit=50)\n134:     password = body.get(\"password\")\n135:     if not isinstance(password, str) or not password:\n136:         errors[\"password\"] = \"Password is required.\"\n137:     elif len(password) > 256:\n138:         errors[\"password\"] = \"Password must be 256 characters or fewer.\"\n139:     elif registering and len(password) < 8:\n140:         errors[\"password\"] = \"Password must be at least 8 characters.\"\n141:     if registering and username and len(username) < 3:\n142:         errors[\"username\"] = \"Username must be at least 3 characters.\"\n143:     return username, password, errors\n144: \n145: \n146: def customer_fields(body):\n147:     errors = {}\n148:     fields = {\n149:         key: validate_text(\n150:             body,\n151:             key,\n152:             errors,\n153:             required=key == \"name\",\n154:             limit=10000 if key == \"notes\" else 255,\n155:         )\n156:         for key in (\"name\", \"email\", \"phone\", \"company\", \"notes\")\n157:     }\n158:     if fields[\"email\"] and not re.fullmatch(\n159:         r\"[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+\", fields[\"email\"]\n160:     ):\n161:         errors[\"email\"] = \"Enter a valid email address.\"\n162:     return fields, errors\n163: \n164: \n165: def find_customer(customer_id):\n166:     row = (\n167:         get_db()\n168:         .execute(CUSTOMER_SELECT + \" WHERE c.id = ? GROUP BY c.id\", (customer_id,))\n169:         .fetchone()\n170:     )\n171:     return dict(row) if row else None\n172: \n173: \n174: def create_app(config=None):\n175:     app = Flask(__name__, static_folder=None)\n176:     app.config.update(\n177:         DATABASE=os.environ.get(\n178:             \"DATABASE_PATH\", str(Path.cwd() / \"data\" / \"directory.sqlite3\")\n179:         ),\n180:         MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH=128 * 1024,\n181:     )\n182:     if config:\n183:         app.config.update(config)\n184:     Path(app.config[\"DATABASE\"]).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n185:     with app.app_context():\n186:         db = get_db()\n187:         db.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n188:         db.executescript(SCHEMA)\n189:         db.close()\n190:         g.pop(\"db\", None)\n191: \n192:     @app.teardown_appcontext\n193:     def close_db(exception=None):\n194:         db = g.pop(\"db\", None)\n195:         if db is not None:\n196:             db.close()\n197: \n198:     @app.after_request\n199:     def response_headers(response):\n200:         response.headers[\"X-Content-Type-Options\"] = \"nosniff\"\n201:         response.headers[\"Referrer-Policy\"] = \"same-origin\"\n202:         response.headers[\"X-Frame-Options\"] = \"DENY\"\n203:         if request.path.startswith(\"/api\"):\n204:             response.headers[\"Cache-Control\"] = \"no-store\"\n205:         return response\n206: \n207:     @app.errorhandler(HTTPException)\n208:     def http_error(exception):\n209:         if request.path.startswith(\"/api\"):\n210:             return error(exception.description, exception.code)\n211:         return exception\n212: \n213:     @app.get(\"/api/health\")\n214:     def health():\n215:         return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n216: \n217:     @app.post(\"/api/auth/register\")\n218:     def register():\n219:         body = json_body()\n220:         if body is None:\n221:             return error(\"Send a JSON object.\")\n222:         username, password, errors = credentials(body, registering=True)\n223:         if errors:\n224:             return error(\"Please check the highlighted fields.\", errors=errors)\n225:         db = get_db()\n226:         try:\n227:             with db:\n228:                 cursor = db.execute(\n229:                     \"INSERT INTO users (username, password_hash, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n230:                     (username, generate_password_hash(password), timestamp()),\n231:                 )\n232:         except sqlite3.IntegrityError:\n233:             return error(\n234:                 \"This username is already taken.\",\n235:                 409,\n236:                 {\"username\": \"This username is already taken.\"},\n237:             )\n238:         return {\"id\": cursor.lastrowid, \"username\": username}, 201\n239: \n240:     @app.post(\"/api/auth/login\")\n241:     def login():\n242:         body = json_body()\n243:         if body is None:\n244:             return error(\"Send a JSON object.\")\n245:         username, password, errors = credentials(body)\n246:         if errors:\n247:             return error(\"Please check the highlighted fields.\", errors=errors)\n248:         db = get_db()\n249:         user = db.execute(\n250:             \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,)\n251:         ).fetchone()\n252:         if (\n253:             not check_password_hash(\n254:                 user[\"password_hash\"] if user else app.config[\"DUMMY_HASH\"], password\n255:             )\n256:             or user is None\n257:         ):\n258:             return error(\"Incorrect username or password.\", 401)\n259:         token = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n260:         with db:\n261:             db.execute(\"DELETE FROM sessions WHERE expires_at <= ?\", (timestamp(),))\n262:             db.execute(\n263:                 \"INSERT INTO sessions (token_hash, user_id, expires_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n264:                 (\n265:                     hashlib.sha256(token.encode()).hexdigest(),\n266:                     user[\"id\"],\n267:                     timestamp(datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=30)),\n268:                 ),\n269:             )\n270:         return {\"token\": token}\n271: \n272:     @app.get(\"/api/auth/me\")\n273:     @authenticated\n274:     def me():\n275:         return dict(g.user)\n276: \n277:     @app.post(\"/api/auth/logout\")\n278:     @authenticated\n279:     def logout():\n280:         db = get_db()\n281:         with db:\n282:             db.execute(\"DELETE FROM sessions WHERE token_hash = ?\", (g.token_hash,))\n283:         return \"\", 204\n284: \n285:     @app.get(\"/api/overview\")\n286:     @authenticated\n287:     def overview():\n288:         db = get_db()\n289:         stats = db.execute(\n290:             \"\"\"SELECT COUNT(*) AS customers, COUNT(DISTINCT NULLIF(LOWER(company), '')) AS companies,\n291:                (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM interactions) AS interactions,\n292:                (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id) FROM interactions WHERE occurred_at >= ?) AS contacted\n293:                FROM customers\"\"\",\n294:             (timestamp(datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(days=30)),),\n295:         ).fetchone()\n296:         companies = db.execute(\n297:             \"SELECT MIN(company) AS company FROM customers WHERE company IS NOT NULL GROUP BY company COLLATE NOCASE ORDER BY company COLLATE NOCASE\"\n298:         ).fetchall()\n299:         return {**dict(stats), \"company_options\": [row[\"company\"] for row in companies]}\n300: \n301:     @app.get(\"/api/customers\")\n302:     @authenticated\n303:     def list_customers():\n304:         errors = {}\n305:         paging = {}\n306:         for key, default, maximum in ((\"page\", 1, 1000000), (\"page_size\", 20, 100)):\n307:             try:\n308:                 value = int(request.args.get(key, default))\n309:                 if not 1 <= value <= maximum:\n310:                     raise ValueError\n311:                 paging[key] = value\n312:             except (TypeError, ValueError):\n313:                 errors[key] = (\n314:                     f\"{key.replace('_', ' ').capitalize()} must be an integer between 1 and {maximum}.\"\n315:                 )\n316:         if errors:\n317:             return error(\"Invalid pagination.\", errors=errors)\n318:         clauses, params = [], []\n319:         query = request.args.get(\"q\", \"\").strip()\n320:         company = request.args.get(\"company\", \"\").strip()\n321:         if query:\n322:             escaped = (\n323:                 query.replace(\"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\").replace(\"%\", \"\\\\%\").replace(\"_\", \"\\\\_\")\n324:             )\n325:             clauses.append(\n326:                 \"(\"\n327:                 + \" OR \".join(\n328:                     f\"c.{field} LIKE ? ESCAPE '\\\\'\"\n329:                     for field in (\"name\", \"email\", \"phone\", \"company\", \"notes\")\n330:                 )\n331:                 + \")\"\n332:             )\n333:             params.extend([f\"%{escaped}%\"] * 5)\n334:         if company:\n335:             clauses.append(\"c.company = ? COLLATE NOCASE\")\n336:             params.append(company)\n337:         where = \" WHERE \" + \" AND \".join(clauses) if clauses else \"\"\n338:         db = get_db()\n339:         total = db.execute(\n340:             \"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM customers c\" + where, params\n341:         ).fetchone()[0]\n342:         rows = db.execute(\n343:             CUSTOMER_SELECT\n344:             + where\n345:             + \" GROUP BY c.id ORDER BY c.name COLLATE NOCASE, c.id LIMIT ? OFFSET ?\",\n346:             [*params, paging[\"page_size\"], (paging[\"page\"] - 1) * paging[\"page_size\"]],\n347:         ).fetchall()\n348:         return {\"items\": [dict(row) for row in rows], \"total\": total, **paging}\n349: \n350:     @app.post(\"/api/customers\")\n351:     @authenticated\n352:     def add_customer():\n353:         return save_customer()\n354: \n355:     @app.put(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>\")\n356:     @authenticated\n357:     def update_customer(customer_id):\n358:         if find_customer(customer_id) is None:\n359:             return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n360:         return save_customer(customer_id)\n361: \n362:     def save_customer(customer_id=None):\n363:         body = json_body()\n364:         if body is None:\n365:             return error(\"Send a JSON object.\")\n366:         fields, errors = customer_fields(body)\n367:         if errors:\n368:             return error(\"Please check the highlighted fields.\", errors=errors)\n369:         db = get_db()\n370:         try:\n371:             with db:\n372:                 if customer_id is None:\n373:                     cursor = db.execute(\n374:                         \"INSERT INTO customers (name, email, phone, company, notes, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n375:                         (*fields.values(), timestamp()),\n376:                     )\n377:                     customer_id = cursor.lastrowid\n378:                     status = 201\n379:                 else:\n380:                     cursor = db.execute(\n381:                         \"UPDATE customers SET name = ?, email = ?, phone = ?, company = ?, notes = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n382:                         (*fields.values(), customer_id),\n383:                     )\n384:                     if not cursor.rowcount:\n385:                         return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n386:                     status = 200\n387:         except sqlite3.IntegrityError:\n388:             return error(\n389:                 \"A customer with this email already exists.\",\n390:                 409,\n391:                 {\"email\": \"A customer with this email already exists.\"},\n392:             )\n393:         return find_customer(customer_id), status\n394: \n395:     @app.get(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>\")\n396:     @authenticated\n397:     def get_customer(customer_id):\n398:         return find_customer(customer_id) or error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n399: \n400:     @app.delete(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>\")\n401:     @authenticated\n402:     def delete_customer(customer_id):\n403:         db = get_db()\n404:         with db:\n405:             cursor = db.execute(\"DELETE FROM customers WHERE id = ?\", (customer_id,))\n406:         if not cursor.rowcount:\n407:             return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n408:         return \"\", 204\n409: \n410:     @app.get(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>/interactions\")\n411:     @authenticated\n412:     def list_interactions(customer_id):\n413:         if find_customer(customer_id) is None:\n414:             return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n415:         rows = (\n416:             get_db()\n417:             .execute(\n418:                 \"\"\"SELECT i.id, i.customer_id, i.kind, i.summary, i.occurred_at, u.username AS logged_by\n419:                FROM interactions i JOIN users u ON u.id = i.user_id WHERE i.customer_id = ?\n420:                ORDER BY i.occurred_at DESC, i.id DESC\"\"\",\n421:                 (customer_id,),\n422:             )\n423:             .fetchall()\n424:         )\n425:         return {\"items\": [dict(row) for row in rows]}\n426: \n427:     @app.post(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>/interactions\")\n428:     @authenticated\n429:     def add_interaction(customer_id):\n430:         if find_customer(customer_id) is None:\n431:             return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n432:         body = json_body()\n433:         if body is None:\n434:             return error(\"Send a JSON object.\")\n435:         errors = {}\n436:         kind = validate_text(body, \"kind\", errors, required=True)\n437:         summary = validate_text(body, \"summary\", errors, required=True, limit=10000)\n438:         if kind not in (\"call\", \"email\", \"meeting\"):\n439:             errors[\"kind\"] = \"Choose call, email, or meeting.\"\n440:         occurred_at = timestamp()\n441:         if \"occurred_at\" in body:\n442:             try:\n443:                 value = datetime.fromisoformat(body[\"occurred_at\"])\n444:                 if value.tzinfo is None:\n445:                     value = value.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n446:                 occurred_at = timestamp(value)\n447:             except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\n448:                 errors[\"occurred_at\"] = \"Enter a valid ISO 8601 date and time.\"\n449:         if errors:\n450:             return error(\"Please check the highlighted fields.\", errors=errors)\n451:         db = get_db()\n452:         try:\n453:             with db:\n454:                 cursor = db.execute(\n455:                     \"INSERT INTO interactions (customer_id, kind, summary, occurred_at, user_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n456:                     (customer_id, kind, summary, occurred_at, g.user[\"id\"]),\n457:                 )\n458:         except sqlite3.IntegrityError:\n459:             return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n460:         return {\n461:             \"id\": cursor.lastrowid,\n462:             \"customer_id\": customer_id,\n463:             \"kind\": kind,\n464:             \"summary\": summary,\n465:             \"occurred_at\": occurred_at,\n466:             \"logged_by\": g.user[\"username\"],\n467:         }, 201\n468: \n469:     @app.get(\"/\")\n470:     @app.get(\"/<path:path>\")\n471:     def frontend(path=\"index.html\"):\n472:         if path == \"api\" or path.startswith(\"api/\"):\n473:             return error(\"API endpoint not found.\", 404)\n474:         if (DIST / path).is_file():\n475:             return send_from_directory(DIST, path)\n476:         return send_from_directory(DIST, \"index.html\")\n477: \n478:     app.config[\"DUMMY_HASH\"] = generate_password_hash(secrets.token_hex(32))\n479:     return app\n480: \n481: \n482: app = create_app()\n483: \n484: \n485: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n486:     app.run(host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=int(os.environ.get(\"PORT\", 8000)))\n\n(End of file - total 486 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import hashlib\nimport os\nimport re\nimport secrets\nimport sqlite3\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom functools import wraps\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom flask import Flask, g, request, send_from_directory\nfrom werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException\nfrom werkzeug.security import check_password_hash, generate_password_hash\n\nDIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\nCUSTOMER_SELECT = \"\"\"\n    SELECT c.*, COUNT(i.id) AS interaction_count,\n           MAX(i.occurred_at) AS last_contacted_at\n    FROM customers c LEFT JOIN interactions i ON i.customer_id = c.id\n\"\"\"\nSCHEMA = \"\"\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/backend/app.py","text":"import hashlib\nimport os\nimport re\nimport secrets\nimport sqlite3\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom functools import wraps\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom flask import Flask, g, request, send_from_directory\nfrom werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException\nfrom werkzeug.security import check_password_hash, generate_password_hash\n\nDIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\nCUSTOMER_SELECT = \"\"\"\n    SELECT c.*, COUNT(i.id) AS interaction_count,\n           MAX(i.occurred_at) AS last_contacted_at\n    FROM customers c LEFT JOIN interactions i ON i.customer_id = c.id\n\"\"\"\nSCHEMA = \"\"\"\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    username TEXT NOT NULL COLLATE NOCASE UNIQUE,\n    password_hash TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (\n    token_hash TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    user_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    expires_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS customers (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    email TEXT COLLATE NOCASE UNIQUE,\n    phone TEXT,\n    company TEXT,\n    notes TEXT,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS interactions (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    customer_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES customers(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    kind TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(kind IN ('call', 'email', 'meeting')),\n    summary TEXT NOT NULL,\n    occurred_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n    user_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id)\n);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS customer_name ON customers(name COLLATE NOCASE);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS customer_company ON customers(company COLLATE NOCASE);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS interaction_customer ON interactions(customer_id, occurred_at DESC);\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef timestamp(value=None):\n    return (\n        (value or datetime.now(timezone.utc))\n        .astimezone(timezone.utc)\n        .isoformat(timespec=\"microseconds\")\n        .replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n    )\n\n\ndef get_db():\n    if \"db\" not in g:\n        from flask import current_app\n\n        g.db = sqlite3.connect(current_app.config[\"DATABASE\"], timeout=30)\n        g.db.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n        g.db.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n    return g.db\n\n\ndef error(message, status=400, errors=None):\n    result = {\"error\": message}\n    if errors:\n        result[\"errors\"] = errors\n    return result, status\n\n\ndef authenticated(view):\n    @wraps(view)\n    def wrapped(*args, **kwargs):\n        parts = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\").split()\n        if len(parts) != 2 or parts[0].lower() != \"bearer\":\n            return error(\"Please sign in to continue.\", 401)\n        token_hash = hashlib.sha256(parts[1].encode()).hexdigest()\n        user = (\n            get_db()\n            .execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT u.id, u.username FROM sessions s JOIN users u ON u.id = s.user_id\n               WHERE s.token_hash = ? AND s.expires_at > ?\"\"\",\n                (token_hash, timestamp()),\n            )\n            .fetchone()\n        )\n        if user is None:\n            return error(\"Your session has expired. Please sign in again.\", 401)\n        g.user = user\n        g.token_hash = token_hash\n        return view(*args, **kwargs)\n\n    return wrapped\n\n\ndef json_body():\n    body = request.get_json(silent=True)\n    return body if isinstance(body, dict) else None\n\n\ndef validate_text(body, field, errors, required=False, limit=255):\n    value = body.get(field)\n    label = field.replace(\"_\", \" \").capitalize()\n    if value is None and not required:\n        return None\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        errors[field] = (\n            f\"{label} must be text.\" if value is not None else f\"{label} is required.\"\n        )\n        return None\n    value = value.strip()\n    if not value:\n        if required:\n            errors[field] = f\"{label} is required.\"\n        return None\n    if len(value) > limit:\n        errors[field] = f\"{label} must be {limit} characters or fewer.\"\n    return value\n\n\ndef credentials(body, registering=False):\n    errors = {}\n    username = validate_text(body, \"username\", errors, required=True, limit=50)\n    password = body.get(\"password\")\n    if not isinstance(password, str) or not password:\n        errors[\"password\"] = \"Password is required.\"\n    elif len(password) > 256:\n        errors[\"password\"] = \"Password must be 256 characters or fewer.\"\n    elif registering and len(password) < 8:\n        errors[\"password\"] = \"Password must be at least 8 characters.\"\n    if registering and username and len(username) < 3:\n        errors[\"username\"] = \"Username must be at least 3 characters.\"\n    return username, password, errors\n\n\ndef customer_fields(body):\n    errors = {}\n    fields = {\n        key: validate_text(\n            body,\n            key,\n            errors,\n            required=key == \"name\",\n            limit=10000 if key == \"notes\" else 255,\n        )\n        for key in (\"name\", \"email\", \"phone\", \"company\", \"notes\")\n    }\n    if fields[\"email\"] and not re.fullmatch(\n        r\"[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+\", fields[\"email\"]\n    ):\n        errors[\"email\"] = \"Enter a valid email address.\"\n    return fields, errors\n\n\ndef find_customer(customer_id):\n    row = (\n        get_db()\n        .execute(CUSTOMER_SELECT + \" WHERE c.id = ? GROUP BY c.id\", (customer_id,))\n        .fetchone()\n    )\n    return dict(row) if row else None\n\n\ndef create_app(config=None):\n    app = Flask(__name__, static_folder=None)\n    app.config.update(\n        DATABASE=os.environ.get(\n            \"DATABASE_PATH\", str(Path.cwd() / \"data\" / \"directory.sqlite3\")\n        ),\n        MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH=128 * 1024,\n    )\n    if config:\n        app.config.update(config)\n    Path(app.config[\"DATABASE\"]).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with app.app_context():\n        db = get_db()\n        db.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\n        db.executescript(SCHEMA)\n        db.close()\n        g.pop(\"db\", None)\n\n    @app.teardown_appcontext\n    def close_db(exception=None):\n        db = g.pop(\"db\", None)\n        if db is not None:\n            db.close()\n\n    @app.after_request\n    def response_headers(response):\n        response.headers[\"X-Content-Type-Options\"] = \"nosniff\"\n        response.headers[\"Referrer-Policy\"] = \"same-origin\"\n        response.headers[\"X-Frame-Options\"] = \"DENY\"\n        if request.path.startswith(\"/api\"):\n            response.headers[\"Cache-Control\"] = \"no-store\"\n        return response\n\n    @app.errorhandler(HTTPException)\n    def http_error(exception):\n        if request.path.startswith(\"/api\"):\n            return error(exception.description, exception.code)\n        return exception\n\n    @app.get(\"/api/health\")\n    def health():\n        return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/auth/register\")\n    def register():\n        body = json_body()\n        if body is None:\n            return error(\"Send a JSON object.\")\n        username, password, errors = credentials(body, registering=True)\n        if errors:\n            return error(\"Please check the highlighted fields.\", errors=errors)\n        db = get_db()\n        try:\n            with db:\n                cursor = db.execute(\n                    \"INSERT INTO users (username, password_hash, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n                    (username, generate_password_hash(password), timestamp()),\n                )\n        except sqlite3.IntegrityError:\n            return error(\n                \"This username is already taken.\",\n                409,\n                {\"username\": \"This username is already taken.\"},\n            )\n        return {\"id\": cursor.lastrowid, \"username\": username}, 201\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/auth/login\")\n    def login():\n        body = json_body()\n        if body is None:\n            return error(\"Send a JSON object.\")\n        username, password, errors = credentials(body)\n        if errors:\n            return error(\"Please check the highlighted fields.\", errors=errors)\n        db = get_db()\n        user = db.execute(\n            \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,)\n        ).fetchone()\n        if (\n            not check_password_hash(\n                user[\"password_hash\"] if user else app.config[\"DUMMY_HASH\"], password\n            )\n            or user is None\n        ):\n            return error(\"Incorrect username or password.\", 401)\n        token = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n        with db:\n            db.execute(\"DELETE FROM sessions WHERE expires_at <= ?\", (timestamp(),))\n            db.execute(\n                \"INSERT INTO sessions (token_hash, user_id, expires_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n                (\n                    hashlib.sha256(token.encode()).hexdigest(),\n                    user[\"id\"],\n                    timestamp(datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=30)),\n                ),\n            )\n        return {\"token\": token}\n\n    @app.get(\"/api/auth/me\")\n    @authenticated\n    def me():\n        return dict(g.user)\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/auth/logout\")\n    @authenticated\n    def logout():\n        db = get_db()\n        with db:\n            db.execute(\"DELETE FROM sessions WHERE token_hash = ?\", (g.token_hash,))\n        return \"\", 204\n\n    @app.get(\"/api/overview\")\n    @authenticated\n    def overview():\n        db = get_db()\n        stats = db.execute(\n            \"\"\"SELECT COUNT(*) AS customers, COUNT(DISTINCT NULLIF(LOWER(company), '')) AS companies,\n               (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM interactions) AS interactions,\n               (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id) FROM interactions WHERE occurred_at >= ?) AS contacted\n               FROM customers\"\"\",\n            (timestamp(datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(days=30)),),\n        ).fetchone()\n        companies = db.execute(\n            \"SELECT MIN(company) AS company FROM customers WHERE company IS NOT NULL GROUP BY company COLLATE NOCASE ORDER BY company COLLATE NOCASE\"\n        ).fetchall()\n        return {**dict(stats), \"company_options\": [row[\"company\"] for row in companies]}\n\n    @app.get(\"/api/customers\")\n    @authenticated\n    def list_customers():\n        errors = {}\n        paging = {}\n        for key, default, maximum in ((\"page\", 1, 1000000), (\"page_size\", 20, 100)):\n            try:\n                value = int(request.args.get(key, default))\n                if not 1 <= value <= maximum:\n                    raise ValueError\n                paging[key] = value\n            except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                errors[key] = (\n                    f\"{key.replace('_', ' ').capitalize()} must be an integer between 1 and {maximum}.\"\n                )\n        if errors:\n            return error(\"Invalid pagination.\", errors=errors)\n        clauses, params = [], []\n        query = request.args.get(\"q\", \"\").strip()\n        company = request.args.get(\"company\", \"\").strip()\n        if query:\n            escaped = (\n                query.replace(\"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\").replace(\"%\", \"\\\\%\").replace(\"_\", \"\\\\_\")\n            )\n            clauses.append(\n                \"(\"\n                + \" OR \".join(\n                    f\"c.{field} LIKE ? ESCAPE '\\\\'\"\n                    for field in (\"name\", \"email\", \"phone\", \"company\", \"notes\")\n                )\n                + \")\"\n            )\n            params.extend([f\"%{escaped}%\"] * 5)\n        if company:\n            clauses.append(\"c.company = ? COLLATE NOCASE\")\n            params.append(company)\n        where = \" WHERE \" + \" AND \".join(clauses) if clauses else \"\"\n        db = get_db()\n        total = db.execute(\n            \"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM customers c\" + where, params\n        ).fetchone()[0]\n        rows = db.execute(\n            CUSTOMER_SELECT\n            + where\n            + \" GROUP BY c.id ORDER BY c.name COLLATE NOCASE, c.id LIMIT ? OFFSET ?\",\n            [*params, paging[\"page_size\"], (paging[\"page\"] - 1) * paging[\"page_size\"]],\n        ).fetchall()\n        return {\"items\": [dict(row) for row in rows], \"total\": total, **paging}\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/customers\")\n    @authenticated\n    def add_customer():\n        return save_customer()\n\n    @app.put(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>\")\n    @authenticated\n    def update_customer(customer_id):\n        if find_customer(customer_id) is None:\n            return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n        return save_customer(customer_id)\n\n    def save_customer(customer_id=None):\n        body = json_body()\n        if body is None:\n            return error(\"Send a JSON object.\")\n        fields, errors = customer_fields(body)\n        if errors:\n            return error(\"Please check the highlighted fields.\", errors=errors)\n        db = get_db()\n        try:\n            with db:\n                if customer_id is None:\n                    cursor = db.execute(\n                        \"INSERT INTO customers (name, email, phone, company, notes, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                        (*fields.values(), timestamp()),\n                    )\n                    customer_id = cursor.lastrowid\n                    status = 201\n                else:\n                    cursor = db.execute(\n                        \"UPDATE customers SET name = ?, email = ?, phone = ?, company = ?, notes = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n                        (*fields.values(), customer_id),\n                    )\n                    if not cursor.rowcount:\n                        return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n                    status = 200\n        except sqlite3.IntegrityError:\n            return error(\n                \"A customer with this email already exists.\",\n                409,\n                {\"email\": \"A customer with this email already exists.\"},\n            )\n        return find_customer(customer_id), status\n\n    @app.get(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>\")\n    @authenticated\n    def get_customer(customer_id):\n        return find_customer(customer_id) or error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n\n    @app.delete(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>\")\n    @authenticated\n    def delete_customer(customer_id):\n        db = get_db()\n        with db:\n            cursor = db.execute(\"DELETE FROM customers WHERE id = ?\", (customer_id,))\n        if not cursor.rowcount:\n            return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n        return \"\", 204\n\n    @app.get(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>/interactions\")\n    @authenticated\n    def list_interactions(customer_id):\n        if find_customer(customer_id) is None:\n            return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n        rows = (\n            get_db()\n            .execute(\n                \"\"\"SELECT i.id, i.customer_id, i.kind, i.summary, i.occurred_at, u.username AS logged_by\n               FROM interactions i JOIN users u ON u.id = i.user_id WHERE i.customer_id = ?\n               ORDER BY i.occurred_at DESC, i.id DESC\"\"\",\n                (customer_id,),\n            )\n            .fetchall()\n        )\n        return {\"items\": [dict(row) for row in rows]}\n\n    @app.post(\"/api/customers/<int:customer_id>/interactions\")\n    @authenticated\n    def add_interaction(customer_id):\n        if find_customer(customer_id) is None:\n            return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n        body = json_body()\n        if body is None:\n            return error(\"Send a JSON object.\")\n        errors = {}\n        kind = validate_text(body, \"kind\", errors, required=True)\n        summary = validate_text(body, \"summary\", errors, required=True, limit=10000)\n        if kind not in (\"call\", \"email\", \"meeting\"):\n            errors[\"kind\"] = \"Choose call, email, or meeting.\"\n        occurred_at = timestamp()\n        if \"occurred_at\" in body:\n            try:\n                value = datetime.fromisoformat(body[\"occurred_at\"])\n                if value.tzinfo is None:\n                    value = value.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n                occurred_at = timestamp(value)\n            except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\n                errors[\"occurred_at\"] = \"Enter a valid ISO 8601 date and time.\"\n        if errors:\n            return error(\"Please check the highlighted fields.\", errors=errors)\n        db = get_db()\n        try:\n            with db:\n                cursor = db.execute(\n                    \"INSERT INTO interactions (customer_id, kind, summary, occurred_at, user_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                    (customer_id, kind, summary, occurred_at, g.user[\"id\"]),\n                )\n        except sqlite3.IntegrityError:\n            return error(\"Customer not found.\", 404)\n        return {\n            \"id\": cursor.lastrowid,\n            \"customer_id\": customer_id,\n            \"kind\": kind,\n            \"summary\": summary,\n            \"occurred_at\": occurred_at,\n            \"logged_by\": g.user[\"username\"],\n        }, 201\n\n    @app.get(\"/\")\n    @app.get(\"/<path:path>\")\n    def frontend(path=\"index.html\"):\n        if path == \"api\" or path.startswith(\"api/\"):\n            return error(\"API endpoint not found.\", 404)\n        if (DIST / path).is_file():\n            return send_from_directory(DIST, path)\n        return send_from_directory(DIST, \"index.html\")\n\n    app.config[\"DUMMY_HASH\"] = generate_password_hash(secrets.token_hex(32))\n    return app\n\n\napp = create_app()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app.run(host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=int(os.environ.get(\"PORT\", 8000)))","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":486,"totalLines":486,"truncated":false}},"title":"backend/app.py","time":{"start":1794319755496,"end":1794319755518}},"id":"prt_1c5caa8e4001T1YI7I5TS6zMAs","sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6a66ffe217KTQBOiu6abw","messageID":"msg_1c5ca9bf2001DkpL7BaFDpU7Qk"}}
